        "prompt": "Red Flowers\n\n\nIt is not known\nwhether you are,\nor merely dreaming yourself.\nYou endure.\nAs if someone forgot\nto turn off the night.\n\nYour face\nsplit in two.\nLight and darkness.\nThe red that runs down\ndoes not know\nif it is blood,\nor merely a memory.\n\nThe lines blur,\nas if someone were trying\nto erase your world\nfrom memory.\nYour body is heavier\nthan yesterday.\n\nRed flowers\ngrow out of places\nthat do not exist.\nFrom cracks and fissures\nthat should not be there.\nThey watch.\nToo red.\nToo self-assured.\n\nYou breathe quietly.\nAs if your breath\nmight betray you.\nWith an open mouth\nyou try to cast out\nsomething that grows \nwithout your consent.\n\nThe darkness within you\ndoes not scream.\nIt does not hurt.\nIt simply sits.\nJust like you.\nJust as weary.\nJust as quiet.\n\nThe wall behind you\nis not a wall.\nThe dirt is not dirt.\nClinging days wait\nuntil you feel them once more.\nAn abandoned sketch.\nWith no beginning.\nWith no end.\nWith no decision.\n\nCongealed red.\nFrom unfinished movements,\nfrom unmade gestures,\nfrom a broken dream.\nThe night\npoured into your depths,\nwhich someone forgot to spill out.\n\nYou wait\nfor something to finally break\nin the right place.\nBut the breath does not return.\n\nAnd only the flowers\nknow\nthat you are trying.\n\n--  \nLyrics: Sadness by the Sea\n",
