    "prompt": "Verse 1\nI see the shadows on the wall,\nThey follow everywhere I go.\nA choice I made, a word I said,\nStill echoes louder than you know.\nI try to leave it in the past,\nBut every night it finds me there,\nA memory I can't outrun,\nA burden that's too hard to bear.\n\nPre-Chorus\nIf I could turn back time somehow,\nI'd change the path I took back then.\nBut all that's left are silent thoughts\nAnd wishing I could make amends.\n\nChorus\n'Cause I'm carrying this weight,\nAnd it's getting hard to breathe.\nEvery mistake I've ever made\nFeels tangled up in me.\nI never meant to cause this pain,\nI never meant to let you down.\nBut guilt is like a storm inside\nThat keeps on pulling me down.\n\nVerse 2\nI hear your voice inside my head,\nThe way things used to be before.\nI wonder if you'll ever know\nHow much I've thought about it all.\nThe hardest thing is facing up\nTo all the damage that I've done.\nNo excuses left to hide behind,\nNo place left to run.\n\nPre-Chorus\nI'd give anything to take it back,\nTo erase the hurt I made.\nBut all I have is honesty\nAnd the debt I haven't paid.\n\nChorus\n'Cause I'm carrying this weight,\nAnd it's getting hard to breathe.\nEvery mistake I've ever made\nFeels tangled up in me.\nI never meant to cause this pain,\nI never meant to let you down.\nBut guilt is like a storm inside\nThat keeps on pulling me down.\n\nBridge\nMaybe healing starts with truth,\nMaybe change begins today.\nI can't undo what happened then,\nBut I can learn from my mistakes.\n\nFinal Chorus\nI'm carrying this weight,\nBut I won't let it define me.\nI'll face the things I've done before\nAnd become who I should be.\nThe past will always be a part\nOf every lesson that I've found.\nAnd though the guilt still lingers here,\nI won't let it drag me down.",
