    "prompt": "[Intro]\n\n[Instrumental]\n\n[Verse 1]\nI felt the pull of minor keys at night,\nBach and Beethoven burning cold and bright.\nNo classical records — only pop inside our wooden walls,\njust village noise and heavy, endless calls.\n\nSnow to be cleared, water to be hauled,\npotato fields where beetles had to crawl.\nPiano dreams were treated as a joke,\nand music from a squeeze-box filled the smoke.\n\n[Pre-chorus 1]\nThe gift arrived in leather, black and new,\nbut stayed untouched — we never saw it through.\n\n[Chorus]\nWe never learned the keys that mattered most,\nthey gathered dust — we drank to every ghost.\nThe choir sang on, but the voices broke,\neach wedding drowned in dusty folk.\nThe dark is louder now.\n\n[Instrumental]\n\n[Verse 2]\nMy brother dragged the heavy case through snow,\nthen left it when the spring began to grow.\nGrandmother's notebook held the old, lost songs,\nher crooked writing where the heart belongs.\n\nThe village praised the man who played for pay,\nand raised their glasses till the night turned grey.\nWe traded fugues for bottles without end,\nand called it sport — the only game we'd tend.\n\n[Pre-chorus 2]\nThe white and black keys waited in the wardrobe,\nwhile we grew used to living with the weight we'd grow.\n\n[Chorus]\nWe never learned the keys that mattered most,\nthey gathered dust — we drank to every ghost.\nThe choir sang on, but the voices broke,\neach wedding drowned in dusty folk.\nThe dark is louder now.\n\n[Bridge (spoken, over quiet, fracturing drums)]\nGrandmother's blue notebook held the songs we'd lost,\nher crooked script — a ghost we couldn't cross.\nWe measured life in buckets, litres, and in snow,\nand called it sport — the only game we'd know.\nOne by one the buttons lost their spring,\none by one we learned to drink and sing.\n\n[Final Chorus]\nWe never learned the keys that mattered most,\nthey gathered dust — we drank to every ghost.\nThe white keys yellow, and the black keys crack,\nthe music sleeps inside a leather sack.\nThe dark is louder now.\n\n[Outro]\n[fade]\n\n[End]",
