    "created_at": "2026-04-16T23:15:00.462Z",
    "prompt": "[Genre: Grunge, Alternative Rock, Nostalgic Rock]\n[Mood: Nostalgic, Energetic, Hypnotic, Bittersweet, Anthemic]\n[Tempo: 95 BPM (driving but not rushed)]\n[Key: D minor (verses) → F major (chorus lift)]\n[Vocal Style: Clean tenor with rasp, angsty, dynamic, raw, emotional]\n[Instrumentation: Downtuned guitar, fuzzed bass, trashy drums with ride bell, feedback swells, half-time breakdown]\n[Themes: 1990s Myrtle Beach, Ocean Boulevard, teenage memories, salt air, arcades, first love, boardwalk, summer freedom]\n\n[Intro - distant feedback, then a single distorted guitar chord, clean arpeggio]\n(Whispered)\nThe boardwalk still hums… even when you're gone.\n\n[Verse 1 - low, gritty, hypnotic syncopation]\nSalt-crusted sneakers on a pavement that never sleeps\nThe ocean's breathing heavy while the arcade beeps\nNeon bleeding orange across a purple sky\nA girl with kohl-rimmed eyes just let her hair dry\nWe were kings of the putt-putt, losers of the claw\nThrowing pennies at the moon from the Pavilion's jaw\nThe Skyscraper rattled, the log ride sprayed\nWe were broke and beautiful and unafraid\n\n[Pre-Chorus - building, drums open up]\nEvery summer burned like a stolen cigarette\nToo fast, too bright, too easy to forget\nBut I still feel the concrete vibrating through my shoes\nWhen I close my eyes… I'm still seventeen with you\n\n[Chorus - explosive, anthemic, full power chords]\nNEON AND SALTWATER – RUNNING DOWN MY SKIN\nTHE BOULEVARD IS CALLING LIKE A SONG I'M STUCK WITHIN\nEVERY BROKEN BOTTLE, EVERY FADING NEON SIGN\nI CAN TASTE THE BOARDWARD FRIES AND THE TANG OF YOUR LIPS ON MINE\nNEON AND SALTWATER – IT NEVER REALLY DIES\nJUST A GHOST IN A HOODIE UNDER SALTWATER SKIES\nYEAH, THE BEACH STILL REMEMBERS, EVEN IF I TRY TO RUN\nNEON AND SALTWATER – YOU WERE THE ONLY ONE\n\n[Verse 2 - more aggressive, driving rhythm]\nRock Burger's grease-stained napkins, Crazy Horse's neon mare\nWe were too young for the show but we didn't care\nStole a six-pack from the Pantry, drank it by the pier\nWatched the jellyfish glow like they had nothing to fear\nYour hair smelled like coconut and cheap motel shampoo\nWe made out on the lifeguard stand 'til the sky turned blue\nThe seagulls judged us, the cops drove slow\nWe were just a couple of kids with nowhere else to go\n\n[Pre-Chorus - repeat, more desperate]\nEvery summer burned like a stolen cigarette\nToo fast, too bright, too easy to forget\nNow I'm 500 miles away in a rain-soaked town\nAnd I'd kill to feel that boardwalk shake when the sun goes down\n\n[Chorus - repeat, higher intensity]\nNEON AND SALTWATER – RUNNING DOWN MY SKIN\nTHE BOULEVARD IS CALLING LIKE A SONG I'M STUCK WITHIN\nEVERY BROKEN BOTTLE, EVERY FADING NEON SIGN\nI CAN TASTE THE BOARDWARK FRIES AND THE TANG OF YOUR LIPS ON MINE\nNEON AND SALTWATER – IT NEVER REALLY DIES\nJUST A GHOST IN A HOODIE UNDER SALTWATER SKIES\nYEAH, THE BEACH STILL REMEMBERS, EVEN IF I TRY TO RUN\nNEON AND SALTWATER – YOU WERE THE ONLY ONE\n\n[Bridge - half-time, spoken-sung, raw and intimate, over a single feedback note]\nI went back last summer… everything was different.\nThe Pavilion's gone. The Crazy Horse is a souvenir shop.\nBut the salt still tastes the same.\nAnd I swear, for one second… I heard your laugh in the waves.\nWe didn't know we were making memories.\nWe were just trying to survive the heat.\nBut God… what a beautiful fire.\n\n[Guitar Solo - melodic, soaring, emotional, with a raw, unpolished tone]\n\n[Outro Chorus - slower, more resigned, with a fading vocal]\nNeon and saltwater… running down my skin\nThe Boulevard is quiet now… but I'm still stuck within\nEvery broken bottle… every faded sign\n(I can taste the boardwalk fries… and the tang of your lips on mine)\nNeon and saltwater… it never really dies\nJust a ghost in a hoodie… under saltwater skies\n\n[Outro - clean arpeggio, distant feedback, then silence]\n(Whispered)\nThe boardwalk still hums…\n(Soft crash cymbal)\nEven when you're gone.",
